  "problem_statement": "*** Problem Statement ***\n\nThe Minority Game\n\nConsider a symmetric game with three players. Each player must simultaneously choose one of two rooms: Room A or Room B.The Payoff Rule:A player wins $1$ if they are the only person in their chosen room. If more than one person chooses the same room, all players in that room receive a payoff of $0$.\n\n\nProblem\n1. Compute all Pure Nash Equilibria. \n2. Compute all mixed Nash Equilibria.  \n",
  "other_prompts": [],
  "current_iteration": 0,
